-- title:
--   Forms with integral Hecke translates span S₂(Γ_H(M))
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive integer and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for the congruence subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, namely the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the set of $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower-right entry reduces modulo $M$ to an element of $H$, and let $\mathbb{T}=$ [`CuspForm.heckeRingH M H 2`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L37) be the subring of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\,S_2(\Gamma_H(M))$ generated by the operators in the range of [`CuspForm.heckeGenH`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L20) for the empty set of excluded primes: the operators `heckeTLinH` attached to primes $\ell\nmid M$, the operators `heckeULinH` attached to the indices $q$ occurring in the `.U` constructor of `Gen M ∅`, and the diamond operators `diamondLinH` attached to elements $d$. For a cusp form $g$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ let $a_n(g)=$ [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) $(\,\underline{\ \ }\,)$ be the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of width $1$ of the underlying function on $\mathbb{H}$. The assertion is that the $\mathbb{C}$-linear span of the set of those $f\in S_2(\Gamma_H(M))$ for which $a_n(tf)$ lies in the image of $\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{C}$ for every $t\in\mathbb{T}$ and every $n\in\mathbb{N}$ is the whole of $S_2(\Gamma_H(M))$.
--
--   This is Shimura's theorem that the cusp forms of weight two on $\Gamma_H(M)$ whose Hecke translates all have integral Fourier expansions at $\infty$ form a full lattice, in the shape produced by Eichler–Shimura theory via the action of the Hecke ring on parabolic cohomology with integral coefficients. It underlies the subsequent construction of an integral, Hecke-stable structure on $S_2(\Gamma_H(M))$ and its comparison with the two-cusp lattice, which are used in the passage from cusp forms to $\mathbb{Q}$-rational eigenforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_span_setOf_forall_heckeRingH_qCoeff_intCast_eq_top.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
